le is to analyze some of the interventions of the Syriac translator – omissions, changes, additions – in his version of the &lt;i&gt;Scholia&lt;/i&gt; on &lt;i&gt;De divinis nominibus&lt;/i&gt;, as it is conserved in the MS &lt;i&gt;Brit. Libr.&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;Add.&lt;/i&gt; 12151 (Wright 625). In this way, it will be possible to identify some specific preoccupations of Phocas, including those of a terminological and doctrinal nature.</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
